Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; explorer7_uninstall.reg
; Reverts explorer7_install.reg by removing every value it added, including
; VerifierFlags and MitigationOptions. Leaving MitigationOptions behind keeps
; CFG forced off for stock explorer.exe.
; The (now empty) explorer.exe IFEO subkey is left in place so any other
; IFEO settings on explorer.exe are untouched. Run as Administrator, then
; sign out / restart explorer.exe for it to take effect.
;
; If you instead want the whole subkey gone, replace the block below with:
;   [-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options\explorer.exe]

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Image File Execution Options\explorer.exe]
"GlobalFlag"=-
"VerifierDlls"=-
"Explorer7Path"=-
"VerifierFlags"=-
"MitigationOptions"=-
